Title: Sort ArrayList of custom Objects by property.
Body: <p>I read about sorting ArrayLists using a Comparator but in all of the examples people used <code>compareTo</code> which according to some research is a method for Strings.</p>

<p>I wanted to sort an ArrayList of custom objects by one of their properties: a Date object
(<code>getStartDay()</code>). Normally I compare them by <code>item1.getStartDate().before(item2.getStartDate())</code> so I was wondering whether I could write something like:</p>

<pre><code>public class CustomComparator {
    public boolean compare(Object object1, Object object2) {
        return object1.getStartDate().before(object2.getStartDate());
    }
}

public class RandomName {
    ...
    Collections.sort(Database.arrayList, new CustomComparator);
    ...
}
</code></pre>

Answers:
```java
import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.time.format.DateTimeFormatter;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Collections;
import java.util.Comparator;

public class CustomComparator {
    public boolean compare(Object object1, Object object2) {
        return ((LocalDate) object1).before((LocalDate) object2);
    }
}

public class RandomName {
    private ArrayList<CustomObject> database;

    public RandomName() {
        this.database = new ArrayList<>();
        // Initialize database with custom objects
    }

    public void addCustomObject(CustomObject customObject) {
        database.add(customObject);
    }

    public void sortDatabaseByStartDate() {
        Collections.sort(database, new CustomComparator());
    }
}

class CustomObject {
    private LocalDate startDate;

    public CustomObject(LocalDate startDate) {
        this.startDate = startDate;
    }

    public LocalDate getStartDate() {
        return startDate;
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        RandomName randomName = new RandomName();
        randomName.addCustomObject(new CustomObject(LocalDate.of(2022, 1, 1)));
        randomName.addCustomObject(new CustomObject(LocalDate.of(2022, 2, 2)));
        randomName.addCustomObject(new CustomObject(LocalDate.of(2022, 3, 3)));

        System.out.println("Before sorting:");
        printDatabase(randomName.database);

        randomName.sortDatabaseByStartDate();

        System.out.println("After sorting:");
        printDatabase(randomName.database);
    }

    public static void printDatabase(ArrayList<CustomObject> database) {
        for (CustomObject customObject : database) {
            System.out.println(customObject.getStartDate());
        }
    }
}
```

